Include <ctime> in exiv2's `src/value.cpp`, which calls `std::mktime`.

exiv2 0.28.9 relies on a transitive include for `std::mktime`. LLVM 23's
libc++ no longer provides it on Linux, so the compile fails there with "no
member named 'mktime' in namespace 'std'" (macOS still gets it transitively).
Drop this patch once the pinned exiv2 includes <ctime> in value.cpp itself
(the patch fails loudly on file-shape changes — desired feedback).

--- a/src/value.cpp
+++ b/src/value.cpp
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include "types.hpp"

 // + standard includes
+#include <ctime>
 #include <sstream>

 // *****************************************************************************
